    "classification":{"subtype":"rwa-treasuries","tags":["tokenized-fund","private-placement","qualified-purchaser","fund-of-funds","cash-management"],"chains":["Ethereum","Polygon","Solana","XRP Ledger"],"jurisdictions":["United States"]},
    "status":{"operating_state":"operating","as_of":"2026-08-03","claim_ids":["claim:ousg:operating-state"]},
    "outcome":{"label":null,"as_of":null,"rule_id":null,"confidence":null,"claim_ids":[]},
    "sections":{
      "what_it_is":"OUSG is the Ondo Short-Term US Government Treasuries Fund, issued by Ondo I LP as limited-partnership interests. The reviewed Form D identifies pooled investment fund interests offered under Rule 506(c) with a section 3(c)(7) exclusion. The token is therefore a restricted fund interest for qualified purchasers, not a permissionless Treasury token.",
      "what_happened":"OUSG began selling interests in February 2023, expanded from Ethereum to Polygon, Solana and XRP Ledger, and changed its portfolio from a single exchange-traded-fund wrapper toward several tokenized cash-management funds plus liquidity reserves. Current official product reporting and an independent onchain aggregator show different totals and scopes; both are stored separately rather than combined.",
      "why_this_outcome":"OUSG gives onboarded institutions one controlled interface to several underlying government-securities and cash-management vehicles, daily NAV accounting and around-the-clock stablecoin conversion paths. That design plausibly improves operational access and diversification, while adding another fund, adviser, custody, smart-contract and liquidity layer between an investor and the underlying assets.",
      "strategic_choices":"Ondo chose a multi-manager fund-of-funds portfolio, stablecoin and bank liquidity buffers, NAV appreciation for the accumulating OUSG share, qualified-purchaser gating, and native issuance on several networks. These choices favor controlled liquidity and portfolio flexibility rather than unrestricted transfer or a fixed promised yield.",
      "operating_model":"Ondo I LP holds underlying tokenized Treasury and money-market funds plus bank deposits and stablecoins. Ondo Capital Management advises the fund and Ondo Finance provides tokenization technology. Investors complete KYC and qualified-purchaser onboarding; subscriptions, redemptions, transfers and receipt are limited to approved participants. NAV is generally updated each business day, and instant routes remain subject to limits and service availability.",
      "token_and_value_capture":"Net income from underlying holdings raises OUSG NAV; OUSG does not promise a fixed return. The official product page states a 0.15 percent management fee waived through 2027-01-01 and fund expenses capped at 0.15 percent. Those economics belong to the OUSG fund and adviser relationship; no reviewed evidence supports direct value accrual from OUSG to the separate ONDO token.",
      "counterfactual":"Holding underlying funds or government securities directly could remove an Ondo layer but would forgo OUSG consolidation, tokenization and stablecoin conversion. A single-manager portfolio would be easier to explain but less diversified across service providers. Permissionless transfer would broaden access but conflict with the documented private-fund eligibility model.",
      "risks_and_unknowns":"Investors face possible total loss, private-placement and transfer restrictions, underlying-fund, interest-rate, liquidity, adviser, custody, stablecoin, smart-contract and network risk. Official product value and aggregator onchain value do not currently reconcile because their chain and reporting scopes differ. That gap must remain visible, and observed APY must not be presented as promised return.",
      "lifecycle":"The amended Form D records first sale on 2023-02-06. Ondo announced native Solana deployment in December 2023, Polygon marketplace access in February 2025 and live XRP Ledger issuance in June 2025. OUSG remained active on 2026-08-03 with current product reporting, a dated portfolio schedule and four aggregator-observed network representations.",
      "outlook_and_watch":"Watch reconciliation between official product reporting, underlying holdings and every network representation; changes to eligibility, minimums and instant-liquidity limits; the 2027 fee-waiver expiry; stablecoin and custody dependencies; portfolio diversification; and any evidence connecting OUSG economics to other Ondo products or tokens. Keep OUSG AUM separate from Ondo platform TVL."
    },
